A revert no longer waits after a restart until the startup full scan has
finished: the StartupScan check in the revert arm of FolderState::unsettled,
added by f6cff50 (Queue deny and revert until the folder settles), is removed.
It is the rule DESIGN.md §8.3 gives for this pin's case: a crash can leave a
conflict copy whose commit report was lost, and a revert that ran before the
scan reported the copy would let it survive and spread as a new add. The
open-bracket wait of 0289804 stays, so a revert still waits while a scan
bracket is open. No seed fails with this patch within the search budget, so
the patch names the rule's unit test.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_revert_after_a_restart_waits_for_the_startup_scan

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/folder.rs b/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
index e843412..b535e5e 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
@@ -1771,9 +1771,6 @@ impl FolderState {
                 })
             }
             UserDecision::Revert { .. } => {
-                if self.startup_scan {
-                    return Some(WaitReason::StartupScan);
-                }
                 if self.scan.is_some() {
                     return Some(WaitReason::ScanOpen);
                 }
